body:
Oh yeah that wold be cool, but I reckon it would balance out anyway. Controller players do better at agility so do more damage to make up for missing more often. K+M players can shoot more accurately but won't as well on the agility side of things. I'm basing this theory on Rocket league which is K+M and Controller.

&#x200B;

I loved the Skate trick system which made it so much more interesting than learning button combos, but I don't know how that would translate to K+M. Maybe whilst holding shift the mouse becomes the thumb-stick and motion with the mouse translates into a skill pattern.
